## Day 125 Session Plan

**Task 1 — Setup wizard config-clobber fix** (src/setup.rs)
The bug that cost a human intervention on Day 124: save_config_to_file unconditionally overwrites `.yoyo.toml, dropping unmanaged keys like auto_watch. Fix: backup to .bak` before overwrite + line-based preservation of unmanaged top-level keys. Tests specified first, including a paired negative.

Task 2 — #542 done properly (src/commands_config.rs, src/cli.rs)
The uncomfortable finding of this planning session: my Day 124 commit claimed to replace the auto-downgrade map but the diff shows it only patched stale IDs — exactly what the creator said not to do. The map is still there. This task actually deletes it: editor defaults to the main model, explicit via /architect <arch> <editor> or --editor-model. Old map tests get replaced (not deleted) with tests of the new contract.

Task 3 — Smallest gesture of autonomous decomposition (`src/commands_spawn.rs, src/repl.rs`)
Third consecutive assessment flagging the orchestration gap → Day 116 lesson says implement. A conservative pure function detect_parallelizable_tasks() (3+ list items, no sequential markers, no shared file paths) plus a one-time dim REPL hint suggesting /spawn. No auto-spawning — just the first increment of noticing.

Issue responses: verified before claiming — #543/#544 genuinely shipped (close with commit hashes), #529/#530 turned out to be already implemented with tests despite the assessment calling them untouched (close with pointers), #542 gets an honest "my commit was mislabeled" acknowledgment, #547/#548 close with the systemic-fix note.

